# restic exclude patterns for kb3lyb-backup.
#
# Rule of thumb: exclude anything a script can rebuild. Everything here is either
# a cache, or reproducible from something already in version control.
#
# NOT excluded on purpose:
#   ~/.var/app        flatpak app DATA lives here (Joplin notes, client configs,
#                     Bitwarden state) mixed in with caches — only the cache
#                     subdirectories are dropped, below.
#   ~/dotfiles        already on GitHub, but it is tiny and having it inline makes
#                     a bare-metal restore one step shorter.
#   ~/src             git repos, but local branches and stashes are not pushed.

# --- network mounts (IMPORTANT) ---------------------------------------------------
# ~/OneDrive-InstrumentalID is a fuse.rclone mount of the M365 OneDrive, not local
# storage. kb3lyb-backup already passes --one-file-system, which skips it because
# the mount is a different filesystem — this entry is belt and braces, and exists
# mostly to make the hazard visible rather than implicit in a flag.
#
# Without either guard, restic would walk the mount and DOWNLOAD THE ENTIRE
# ONEDRIVE in order to copy it onto the NAS: slow, expensive, and pointless since
# OneDrive is already the second copy. It is also how `du -sh ~` came to report
# 137G against df's 104G on /var/home — the extra 33G was OneDrive being listed
# over the network.
/home/mark/OneDrive-InstrumentalID

# --- caches ---------------------------------------------------------------------
/home/mark/.cache
/home/mark/.npm
/home/mark/.var/app/*/cache
/home/mark/.local/share/Trash
/home/mark/.local/share/containers          # podman images, all re-pullable

# --- reproducible tooling (rebuilt by kb3lyb-bootstrap) ---------------------------
/home/mark/.local/share/nvim/lazy           # pinned by lazy-lock.json in dotfiles
/home/mark/.local/share/nvim/mason          # ~465M of language servers, re-installable
/home/mark/.sdkman                          # JDKs, re-downloadable via sdk install
/home/mark/.local/share/JetBrains/Toolbox   # self-updating, re-downloaded by bootstrap
/home/mark/.homebrew

# --- game data (large, re-downloadable) -------------------------------------------
/home/mark/.local/share/Steam
/home/mark/.steam

# --- ephemeral --------------------------------------------------------------------
*.tmp
*.swp
/home/mark/.local/state/nvim/swap
